            {'type': 'heading', 'text': 'What Comes Next'},
            "ACPWB is building a public data service that will let other organizations look up an internet address and learn what ACPWB's instruments have concluded about it: a classification and a confidence level, though not how ACPWB knows. Five billion requests, ACPWB has found, are a great deal of evidence about who is on the internet and what they are running, and the organization does not believe it should keep that evidence to itself. It will announce availability when the service is ready.",
            "The service will be run by Gordon Achterberg, newly appointed Director of Readership Verification, whose department is responsible for confirming that ACPWB's readers are who they say they are.",
