            {'type': 'heading', 'text': 'From the CEO'},
            '"Last week I said we should look at our logs more often. We have, and I am told I created a monster," said Margaret Okafor, Chief Executive Officer of ACPWB. "Our traffic told us something was about to change in Vladimir twice, hours before the news did, and it told us from fifty countries at once. I still do not know what that means, and the board has asked me to stop guessing in public. So I will say only this: our research remains free to every reader in every country, whenever they come back, on whatever computer they come back with."',
            "Figures are requests to acpwb.com and its subdomains, located by country, with data through 18:00 UTC on October 16. A normal night is each country's median from September 21 to October 10, measured between 00:00 and 10:00 UTC. The data-center hubs are the United States, Singapore, France, the United Kingdom, Germany, Brazil and China. All times are UTC unless noted.",
